Formatter-closure regression (2026-07-25 amendment), the "default" variant:
without the fix, gsx fmt's word-gap fill could reflow this arm's long prose so
"default:" became the first word on a line — which the parser then reads as a
real default arm, producing a "multiple defaults" codegen failure (the source
never had two). 34 "x" words is one of the exact lengths where the fmt
corpus/property-test width (80 cols) forces a wrap right at that boundary
(found by sweeping word counts 1..100 before picking this one). The printer's
case-body bond keeps "default:" off line start regardless of width, so
re-parsing formatted output still yields exactly one selected arm. Checked by
internal/printer's TestCorpusInputsProperty.
-- input.gsx --
package views

component Prose(k string) {
	<div>{ switch k {
	case "a":
		x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x default: wins
	default:
		<i>y</i>
	} }</div>
}
-- invoke --
Prose("a")
-- diagnostics.golden --
-- render.golden --
<div>x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x default: wins</div>
-- generated.x.go.golden --
